ytop is a minimal interactive process monitor for FreeBSD, designed for
monitoring CPU-bound server applications. Its process list shows CPU usage,
virtual and resident memory sizes, accumulated CPU time, thread counts, and
host or jail domains.

Select a process to view its threads, including user and system CPU usage,
scheduling priorities, thread states, CPU affinity, and context-switch counts
and rates. Keyboard and mouse controls support row selection, scrolling, and
switching between process and thread lists, with an optional per-CPU grid.
